From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:24:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: check WSI PCI endpoints before grouping

A WSI graph can describe a QCN9274 which never enumerated on PCI. The
remaining devices then wait for the missing member before starting
firmware.

Check that each PCI member has an enumerated endpoint while reading the WSI
graph. Use the existing single device group path if a member is missing.
Check enumeration rather than driver binding or firmware readiness so that
probe order and calibration failures do not change group admission. Reject
bridge devices and release temporary device and graph references normally.

Group startup, timeouts and recovery policies remain unchanged.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -2000,6 +2000,22 @@ static struct ath12k_hw_group *ath12k_co
 	return NULL;
 }
 
+static bool ath12k_core_wsi_endpoint_present(struct device_node *node)
+{
+	if (!of_device_is_compatible(node, "pci17cb,1109"))
+		return true;
+
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PCI)
+	struct device *dev __free(put_device) =
+		bus_find_device_by_of_node(&pci_bus_type, node);
+
+	/* Check enumeration, not driver binding or firmware readiness. */
+	return dev && !pci_is_bridge(to_pci_dev(dev));
+#else
+	return false;
+#endif
+}
+
 static int ath12k_core_get_wsi_info(struct ath12k_hw_group *ag,
 				    struct ath12k_base *ab)
 {
@@ -2019,6 +2035,14 @@ static int ath12k_core_get_wsi_info(stru
 			break;
 		}
 
+		if (!ath12k_core_wsi_endpoint_present(wsi_dev)) {
+			ath12k_warn(ab,
+				    "WSI PCI endpoint %pOF not found, using a single device group\n",
+				    wsi_dev);
+			ret = -ENODEV;
+			break;
+		}
+
 		ag->wsi_node[device_count++] = of_node_get(wsi_dev);
 
 		struct device_node *tx_endpoint __free(device_node) =
